ry Human Resources Menu Human Resources New Employee Information Job Opportunities Hiring Process Hiring and Search Forms Hiring Part-Time Adjuncts Hiring Student Workers Hiring University Assistants Hiring Graduate Assistants Hiring Graduate Interns Hiring and Search Manual Payroll Payroll Overview CORE Self-Service (Time Reporting) Payroll Staff ADA Policy ADA/Reasonable Accommodation Requests Employees and Job Applicants Procedures for Requesting a Reasonable Accommodation Request an Employment Accommodation Students, Guests and Visitors to Central Employee Benefits Education Benefits Employee Assistance Program Family & Medical Leave Medical & Dental Miscellaneous Benefits Retirement Workers' Compensation Part-Time Faculty Information Policies Forms Union Contracts Human Resources Staff Contact Information Human Resources Lawrence J. Davidson Hall 201 (860) 832-1756 humanresources-1@mail.ccsu.edu Payroll Lawrence J. Davidson Hall 211 (860) 832-2525 payroll@mail.ccsu.edu Breadcrumb Home Human Resources Part-Time Faculty Information Part-Time Faculty Information AAUP Union Information Dual Employment Employee Related Policies Employee Information Sheet Part-Time Faculty Hiring Forms Part-Time/Full-Time Faculty Appointment Form Medical and Dental Health insurance benefits are available at group rates from Anthem. Dental insurance is available from CIGNA. A break in service of one semester or more will require that you re-enroll to continue participation in a health insurance plan. Note: Pursuant to CGS Section 5-259, the State Comptroller’s Office has issued eligibility guidelines for state subsidized medical and dental insurance coverage for part-time faculty who meet the eligibility requirements and who teach nine (9) or more credits in the aggregate in the Connecticut State University system, the University of Connecticut, or the Community College system. 2026-2027 Active Employees Healthcare Planner 2026-2027 - Health Insurance Rates Health Plan Reimbursement Eligibility Retirement More Information Part-time faculty are allowed a one-time irrevocable election to participate in a State of Connecticut retirement plan. Part-time faculty who are also employed by another state agency and enrolled in a retirement plan must be enrolled in the same retirement plan with Central. Part-time faculty may waive participation in a retirement plan. Please be aware that waiver of retirement plan membership results in ineligibility for retirement membership during any subsequent employment as a part-time lecturer within the Connecticut Higher Education System. Note: Failure to waive or enroll in a retirement plan results in an automatic default to the Hybrid plan with your first paycheck of the semester. Tuition Waiver More Information Note: You must have accrued 18 load hours to be eligible for tuition waiver. The total benefit shall not exceed the member’s current equivalent workload credit and shall only be used during the semester of employment of the semester immediately following. Credit Unions Achieve Financial Credit Union Connecticut State Employees Credit Union 1615 Stanley Street CT 06050 Directions 860.832.3200 Central Facebook Central Twitter Central Instagram Central Linkedin Central YouTube Contact Us Campus Map Athletics Campus Safety Wellness Services Title IX Search Search Main Navigation (Mobile) Home Admissions First-Year Students Transfer Students Graduate Students International Students Adult/Returning Students Accepted Students Visit Central Tuition & Aid Academics Programs & Majors Departments Schools Register for Classes Calendar Student Support Services Student Life Student Affairs Residence Life Dining & Meal Plans Campus Events Student Activities & Leadership Development About Utility Navigation Apply Visit Give Athletics Calendar Blackboard Central Email Campus Map Courses & Programs Faculty/Staff Directory IT Services News Library"
